# Implementation Plan: High-G Impact & Motion Driver

Implement a modular High-G Impact Accelerometer Driver (`src/platform/drivers/high_g/`) for the Nordic Thingy:91 X platform to detect shock events, high-G impacts, free-fall drops, and peak acceleration metrics.

## Proposed Changes

### Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL) - Drivers & Math

#### [NEW] [high_g.h](file:///d:/Projects/thingy91x/src/platform/drivers/high_g/high_g.h)
- Declare `struct high_g_data` containing `accel_x`, `accel_y`, `accel_z` (in g), `magnitude` $\|a\| = \sqrt{a_x^2 + a_y^2 + a_z^2}$, `peak_g`, `impact_detected`, `freefall_detected`, and `valid` flag.
- Expose driver interface functions:
  - `int high_g_init(void)`: Initialize Devicetree sensor node (`adi,adxl372`, `bosch,bma400`) or register software fallback simulation.
  - `int high_g_read(struct high_g_data *data)`: Sample accelerometer channels, compute vector magnitude $\|a\|$, evaluate shock & free-fall thresholds, and update peak hold.
  - `int high_g_set_threshold(float threshold_g)`: Set shock trigger threshold in g.
  - `int high_g_reset_peak(void)`: Clear stored peak acceleration value.
  - `int high_g_sleep(void)`: Put sensor into ultra-low-power suspended state (`CONFIG_PM_DEVICE`).

#### [NEW] [high_g.c](file:///d:/Projects/thingy91x/src/platform/drivers/high_g/high_g.c)
- Implement driver logic using Zephyr `sensor.h` APIs (`SENSOR_CHAN_ACCEL_XYZ`), Devicetree macros (`DT_HAS_COMPAT_STATUS_OKAY`), vector math routines, threshold checks, logging via `LOG_MODULE_REGISTER(high_g_driver)`, POSIX error return codes, and software simulation fallback for off-target validation.

